{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Speaker Recognition & Verification Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: toy embedding from MFCC statistics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def embed_mfcc_stats(signal, sr):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    frames = featurize_mfcc(signal, sr, n_mfcc=13)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mean = [sum(f[i] for f in frames) / len(frames) for i in range(13)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    std = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        math.sqrt(sum((f[i] - mean[i]) ** 2 for f in frames) / len(frames))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(13)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mean + std  # 26-d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Not SOTA by a mile \u2014 for teaching only. `code/main.py` uses this as a proof-of-concept on synthetic speaker data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: cosine similarity + threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cosine(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dot = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    na = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    nb = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dot / (na * nb) if na and nb else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def verify(enroll, test, threshold=0.75):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return cosine(enroll, test) >= threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: EER from similarity pairs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def eer(same_scores, diff_scores):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    thresholds = sorted(set(same_scores + diff_scores))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best = (1.0, 1.0, 0.0)  # (fa, fr, threshold)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for t in thresholds:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        fr = sum(1 for s in same_scores if s < t) / len(same_scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        fa = sum(1 for s in diff_scores if s >= t) / len(diff_scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if abs(fa - fr) < abs(best[0] - best[1]):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best = (fa, fr, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return (best[0] + best[1]) / 2, best[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Returns (eer, threshold_at_eer). Report both."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: production with SpeechBrain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from speechbrain.pretrained import EncoderClassifier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "clf = EncoderClassifier.from_hparams(source=\"speechbrain/spkrec-ecapa-voxceleb\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# enroll: average the embeddings of 3-5 clean samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "enroll = torch.stack([clf.encode_batch(load(x)) for x in enrollment_clips]).mean(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# verify"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "score = clf.similarity(enroll, clf.encode_batch(load(\"test.wav\"))).item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "verdict = score > 0.25   # ECAPA typical threshold; tune on your data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: diarize with pyannote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from pyannote.audio import Pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pipe = Pipeline.from_pretrained(\"pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "diarization = pipe(\"meeting.wav\", num_speakers=None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for turn, _, speaker in diarization.itertracks(yield_label=True):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{turn.start:.1f}\u2013{turn.end:.1f}  {speaker}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Builds synthetic \"speakers\" (different tone profiles), enrolls, computes EER on a 100-pair trial list.\n2. **Medium.** Use SpeechBrain ECAPA on 30 VoxCeleb1 utterances (5 speakers \u00d7 6 each). Compute EER with cosine vs PLDA.\n3. **Hard.** Build the full enroll \u2192 diarize \u2192 verify pipeline with `pyannote.audio`. Evaluate DER on AMI dev set."
      ]
    }
